    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d842">

                <pb facs="1166" n="1038" xml:id="pg1038"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">474.00 R 29/126: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Herrick</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-07-11T16:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11, 1928—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 5:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>187. Reparation 105.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Reference Department’s letter June 12, 1928,<anchor n="9" xml:id="d842-f1"
                        /> and my reply June 28, regarding agreement to be reached for distribution
                        Bulgarian reparation payments. Also my letter June 29<anchor n="9"
                            xml:id="d842-f2"/> concerning Commission’s decision of June 23 as to
                        postponement Bulgarian payments and recommendation that Greece be allotted
                        certain sum out of blocked Bulgarian payments.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>General Secretary has now circulated as matter of urgency protocol
                        prepared by British, French and Italian representatives granting Greek
                        Government on account of earthquake damages a special advance from the
                        Bulgarian blocked payments equal to its reparation percentage fixed in
                        Article 7 of the January 14, 1925, agreement.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d842-f3"
                        /> Meeting of representatives of signatories of January 14, 1925, agreement
                        has been set for morning July 13 to discuss this protocol.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>[Paraphrase.] May I suggest the Department authorize me to advise the
                        General Secretary that, since the United States Government does not
                        participate in reparation payments by Bulgaria, it does not feel called upon
                        to sign a protocol drawn up following the proposed discussions. Early
                        instructions would be appreciated. [End paraphrase.]</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
